@page "/parameters"
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<PageTitle>Parameters & child content</PageTitle>

<h1>Parameters &amp; child content</h1>

<p>
    Components communicate with their parents through <code>[Parameter]</code>
    properties. Rich content is passed via <code>RenderFragment</code>
    parameters (the default one is <em>ChildContent</em>). Events flow back up
    the tree via <code>EventCallback</code>.
</p>

@*
    1. Scalar parameters (Name, Role, Bio) + attribute splatting (style=...).
*@
<h3>1. Reusable component with typed parameters</h3>
<div class="d-flex gap-3 flex-wrap">
    <UserCard Name="Ada Lovelace"
              Role="Mathematician"
              Bio="First computer programmer, arguably."
              style="border-color: teal;" />

    <UserCard Name="Grace Hopper"
              Role="Rear Admiral / Compiler pioneer"
              Bio="Coined the term 'debugging' after a literal moth." />
</div>

@*
    2. ChildContent (a RenderFragment) lets the parent supply arbitrary markup.
       The <Alert> component wraps whatever we put between its tags.
*@
<h3 class="mt-4">2. ChildContent + EventCallback</h3>

<Alert Severity="Alert.AlertSeverity.Warning"
       Dismissible="true"
       OnDismiss="OnAlertDismissed">
    This alert's body is a <strong>RenderFragment</strong>. Click the × to see
    the child fire an <code>EventCallback</code> back up to this page.
</Alert>

<p><em>Status:</em> @status</p>

@code {
    private string status = "Alert visible.";

    // The signature matches the child's EventCallback (no payload here).
    // For a typed payload use EventCallback<T> on both sides.
    private void OnAlertDismissed()
    {
        status = $"Parent was notified at {DateTime.Now:HH:mm:ss}.";
    }
}
